The new graphs use PipeWire's filter-chain and SOFA spatializer (Dmitry
Sharshakov), the upstream HeSuVi channel convention and PSD upmix settings
(PipeWire authors). The passive matrix coefficients and delay follow Steve
Davies' MPlayer surround decoder (GPL-2.0-or-later), whose notice and source
are at https://github.com/pigoz/mplayer-svn/blob/master/libaf/af_surround.c .
This implementation is GPL-3.0-or-later, compatible with that permission.

The MIT KEMAR measurements are by Bill Gardner and Keith Martin, MIT Media
Laboratory, 1994: https://sound.media.mit.edu/resources/KEMAR.html . Their
release allows use without restrictions provided the authors are cited.
The response file is supplied by the libmysofa dependency, not copied here.
libmysofa, by Christian Hoene and its contributors, reads SOFA; PipeWire's
SOFA spatializer performs the convolution. Imported response files stay
owned by the person and are never included in this package.

